---
source: crates/rustman-cli/src/tests.rs
expression: help
---
Serve an OpenAPI document as a mock server until Ctrl+C

Usage: rustman mock serve [OPTIONS] <OPENAPI>

Arguments:
  <OPENAPI>
          The OpenAPI 3.0/3.1 document: a file or an http(s) URL

Options:
      --host <HOST>
          Address to bind: an IP address or localhost (default: [mock] host in rustman.toml, else 127.0.0.1)

      --port <PORT>
          Port to bind; 0 picks a free port (default: [mock] port in rustman.toml, else 4010)

      --allow-remote
          Allow binding an address reachable from the network

      --allow-remote-refs
          Fetch $refs to other http(s) documents

      --seed <N>
          Seed of synthesized bodies (default: [mock] seed, else 0)

      --no-prefer
          Ignore the Prefer request header

      --no-validate
          Do not validate requests against the document

      --enforce-security
          Answer 401 to requests without the credentials their operation declares

      --stateful
          Keep an in-memory store: POST creates, GET reads, PUT/PATCH update, DELETE removes

      --env <NAME>
          Environment holding the [mock.security] expected values and receiving the secrets of --record (default: RUSTMAN_ENV, else the workspace default)

      --workspace <DIR>
          Workspace whose rustman.toml holds [mock] (default: search from the current directory upwards; none means the defaults)

      --cors
          Add CORS headers and answer preflights (default: on for loopback)

      --no-cors
          Never add CORS headers; OPTIONS goes to the document

      --jsonl
          Log each request as one JSON object per line on stdout (the banner goes to stderr)

      --history
          Also record each exchange in history, tagged mock

      --proxy-unmatched <URL>
          Forward requests no operation or override matches to this upstream (only its origin is contacted)

      --record <DIR>
          Save each proxied exchange as a request file in DIR, inside the workspace, with secrets moved to the active environment

      --color <WHEN>
          Color: auto (a terminal without NO_COLOR or TERM=dumb), always or never
          
          [default: auto]

  -v, --verbose...
          Log more on stderr: -v requests, -vv headers, -vvv everything (RUST_LOG, when set, replaces these levels)

  -h, --help
          Print help
